keywords:
  - retrieval-augmented-generation
  - information-retrieval
  - bm25
  - sentence-embeddings
  - reciprocal-rank-fusion
  - sec-edgar
  - evaluation
abstract: "Educational research study building a retrieval-augmented question-answering assistant over two real SEC 10-K filings (Apple, Microsoft), comparing BM25, dense sentence-embedding and reciprocal-rank-fusion hybrid retrieval against a random control with Recall@k/MRR/nDCG, and evaluating citation-grounded generation with a small local instruction-tuned model and an explicit refusal policy."
